<mjml lang="en">
  <mj-head>
    <!--
      PROBE — mobile gutters and caption alignment (2026-08-13).
      Not a catalog page. Send dist/probe_mobile-gutters_live.html through EN
      to EoA and read android16_gmailapp_pixel10_* and iphone17_* first.

      WHY THIS EXISTS — the previous column probe answered the wrong question
      The Gmail-Android "columns shrink" finding does not reproduce. Measured
      from the aBPD6k1l render: Pixel 10 is 1080 device px at DPR 3, so Gmail
      lays the email out at ~333 CSS px. The image measured 251 CSS px, and
      "container minus section padding (32x2) minus column padding (8x2)"
      predicts 252.7 — within 1.7px. The competing model (column padding
      removed) predicts 268.7 and is off by 17.7. Cross-checked against the
      background bands in the same render, which carry no side padding and do
      span the full container.

      So the image already fills its column exactly. What looks like shrinkage
      is 80 CSS px of gutter on a 333 px screen — 24% of the width — and it is
      NOT client-specific: the image/container ratio is 0.755 on Gmail Android
      and 0.746 on iPhone. That is why percent columns, mj-group and inlined
      min-width all measured identically to the control: there was nothing for
      them to fix.

      WHAT IS ACTUALLY UNDECIDED
      How much gutter the design wants on a narrow screen, and whether the
      caption can sit flush with its image. Every variant below is a real
      authoring choice; pick by eye from the renders.

        G1 CONTROL   section 16/32, column 0/8   — today's Story Card.
                     Predicts ~251 CSS px of image on Gmail Android.
        G2 TIGHTER   section 16/16, column 0/8   — halves the section gutter.
                     Predicts ~283. Changes desktop too (536 -> 568 content).
        G3 FLUSH     section 16/0,  column 0/0   — image runs to the email
                     edge. Predicts ~333. Biggest change; desktop card becomes
                     full-bleed, which may not suit every block.
        G4 CSS TEST  markup identical to G1, plus a CLASS-ONLY descendant rule
                     (.probe-flush td) that zeroes side padding below 600px.
                     This is the ONLY variant that could fix mobile without
                     touching desktop — but it is a blunt instrument: it hits
                     EVERY td inside the card, so watch whether the body copy
                     loses its inset too. It also answers a standing question:
                     whether a class-only descendant rule reaches Gmail at all
                     (child combinators are escaped by EN, and attribute
                     selectors are inert in Gmail — see guide 2d).

      READ IT LIKE THIS
      Compare each variant's image width AND whether the caption's left edge
      lines up with the image's left edge. The QA report said captions sit
      "off the edge of the image"; if that reproduces here it will be visible
      as a caption starting left of the photo.

      G4 is the interesting one. If it renders like G3 in Gmail with the body
      copy still readable, CSS can solve this and desktop stays untouched. If
      G4 matches G1 in Gmail, class-only descendant rules do not reach it
      either, and the fix has to be authored (G2 or G3), which is a design
      decision rather than a bug fix.
    -->
    <mj-breakpoint width="600px" />
    <mj-title>PROBE — mobile gutters</mj-title>

    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-text
        color="#000000"
        font-size="18px"
        font-weight="400"
        font-family="Tahoma, sans-serif"
        line-height="24px"
        css-class="wysiwyg"
      />
      <mj-image padding="0" />
      <mj-class name="caption" font-size="10px" line-height="16px" padding="8px 0 0 0" />
    </mj-attributes>

    <mj-style>
      /* G4 only. Class-only + plain descendant: no child combinator (EN
         escapes those) and no attribute selector (inert in Gmail). */
      @media (max-width: 599px) {
        .probe-flush td {
          padding-left: 0 !important;
          padding-right: 0 !important;
        }
      }
    </mj-style>

    <mj-raw>
      <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="format-detection" content="telephone=no" />
    </mj-raw>
    <mj-include path="./styles.css" type="css" />
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body css-class="email-body" background-color="#ffffff">

    <!-- START: Gutter Label G1 -->
    <mj-section css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">G1 — CONTROL (SECTION 32 / COLUMN 8)</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Gutter Label G1 -->

    <!-- START: Gutter G1 Control -->
    <mj-section css-class="two-col-image-text-block block" background-color="#ffffff" padding="16px 32px">
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column first-column" width="240px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-image src="assets/photo-garden.jpg" width="224px" alt="Children exploring plants in a schoolyard garden" padding="0" align="center" fluid-on-mobile="true" css-class="two-col-image" />
        <mj-text mj-class="caption" css-class="caption" align="left">Caption — should sit flush with the photo's left edge.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column" width="296px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-text padding="0 0 8px"><h3 style="margin:0;">G1 control heading.</h3></mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0">Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur. Morbi adipiscing convallis vitae quisque commodo volutpat ut.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Gutter G1 Control -->

    <!-- START: Gutter Label G2 -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">G2 — TIGHTER SECTION (16 / 8)</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Gutter Label G2 -->

    <!-- START: Gutter G2 Tighter -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude css-class="two-col-image-text-block block" background-color="#ffffff" padding="16px 16px">
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column first-column" width="240px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-image src="assets/photo-garden.jpg" width="224px" alt="Children exploring plants in a schoolyard garden" padding="0" align="center" fluid-on-mobile="true" css-class="two-col-image" />
        <mj-text mj-class="caption" css-class="caption" align="left">Caption — should sit flush with the photo's left edge.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column" width="296px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-text padding="0 0 8px"><h3 style="margin:0;">G2 tighter heading.</h3></mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0">Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur. Morbi adipiscing convallis vitae quisque commodo volutpat ut.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Gutter G2 Tighter -->

    <!-- START: Gutter Label G3 -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">G3 — FLUSH (SECTION 0 / COLUMN 0)</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Gutter Label G3 -->

    <!-- START: Gutter G3 Flush -->
    <mj-section css-class="two-col-image-text-block block" background-color="#ffffff" padding="16px 0">
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column first-column" width="240px" vertical-align="top" padding="0">
        <mj-image src="assets/photo-garden.jpg" width="240px" alt="Children exploring plants in a schoolyard garden" padding="0" align="center" fluid-on-mobile="true" css-class="two-col-image" />
        <mj-text mj-class="caption" css-class="caption" align="left" padding="8px 8px 0 8px">Caption — should sit flush with the photo's left edge.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column" width="360px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-text padding="0 0 8px"><h3 style="margin:0;">G3 flush heading.</h3></mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0">Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur. Morbi adipiscing convallis vitae quisque commodo volutpat ut.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Gutter G3 Flush -->

    <!-- START: Gutter Label G4 -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">G4 — G1 + CLASS-ONLY MOBILE RULE</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Gutter Label G4 -->

    <!-- START: Gutter G4 Css Test -->
    <mj-section css-class="two-col-image-text-block block probe-flush" background-color="#ffffff" padding="16px 32px">
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column first-column" width="240px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-image src="assets/photo-garden.jpg" width="224px" alt="Children exploring plants in a schoolyard garden" padding="0" align="center" fluid-on-mobile="true" css-class="two-col-image" />
        <mj-text mj-class="caption" css-class="caption" align="left">Caption — should sit flush with the photo's left edge.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column" width="296px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-text padding="0 0 8px"><h3 style="margin:0;">G4 css-rule heading.</h3></mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0">Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur. Morbi adipiscing convallis vitae quisque commodo volutpat ut.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Gutter G4 Css Test -->

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
